@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About CardCompass Methodology";
}

<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="max-w-800 mx-auto">
        <div class="text-center mb-5">
            <span class="badge bg-primary bg-opacity-10 text-primary fw-bold px-3 py-1 mb-2">Editorial Independence</span>
            <h1 class="h2 fw-bold">Our Philosophy & Methodology</h1>
            <p class="text-muted">How CardCompass evaluates Indian credit cards with transparent mathematics</p>
        </div>

        <div class="cc-surface-card p-4 mb-4">
            <h4 class="h5 fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="bi bi-shield-check text-success me-2"></i> 1. Primary Source Research</h4>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                Every credit card in our catalog is researched directly from official bank disclosures: Most Important Terms and Conditions (MITC), Schedule of Charges, and official issuer product portals. We do not rely on rumors, forum threads, or unverified claims.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cc-surface-card p-4 mb-4">
            <h4 class="h5 fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="bi bi-calculator text-primary me-2"></i> 2. Net Annual Benefit Model</h4>
            <p class="text-muted mb-2">
                We evaluate cards based on real financial return:
            </p>
            <div class="p-3 bg-light rounded text-center fw-bold font-monospace text-dark mb-3">
                Estimated Net Benefit = Total Annual Rewards Earned + Welcome Bonuses - Applicable Annual Fees
            </div>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                We distinguish between reward points and their actual rupee redemption value. For example, a card that earns 10 points per ₹100 where 1 point = ₹0.20 yields an effective return of 2%, whereas a card earning 5 points per ₹150 where 1 point = ₹1 yields 3.33%.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cc-surface-card p-4 mb-4">
            <h4 class="h5 fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="bi bi-funnel text-warning me-2"></i> 3. Accounting for Caps & Exclusions</h4>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                High headline reward percentages mean nothing if they hit a low monthly cap. Our calculation engine incorporates monthly category caps (e.g. Swiggy 10% capped at ₹1,500/month, Airtel 25% capped at ₹250/month) and excludes non-qualifying spend categories like rent, wallet loads, fuel, and government payments.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cc-surface-card p-4">
            <h4 class="h5 fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="bi bi-bank text-info me-2"></i> 4. Honest Disclosures & Unknowns</h4>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                Banks change credit card terms frequently. When a rule is not officially published or has unclear redemption rules, we display "Information unavailable" or "Subject to verification" rather than fabricating numbers.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
